pany\" to avoid placeholders. But formal letter needs sender/recipient? Could include placeholders for names and dates only: e.g. [Date], [Vendor Contact Name], [Vendor Company Name]? Company name is a name? It says names and dates, likely names of people and dates. But \"hardware vendor\" maybe [Vendor Name] is a name. But \"only for names and dates\" means placeholders allowed for names and dates, not for other details. We can use [Vendor Name] as name. But maybe better to avoid bracketed company names by using \"your company\" and \"our company\". But letterhead? Could start:\n\n[Date]\n\n[Vendor Contact Name]\n[Vendor Company Name]\n[Address?] Address not name/date, avoid placeholder. Could omit address.\n\nDear [Vendor Contact Name],\n\n...\n\nSincerely,\n[Your Name]\n[Title]\n[Company Name]? Company name is a name? Could be placeholder. But \"only for names and dates\" maybe [Company Name] okay? It's a name. But if we want strict, use \"our company\" and sign with [Your Name], [Title]. But formal letter usually includes company. Could use \"Small Software Company\"? No.\n\nNeed about 350 words. Let's draft around 350. Count words. Need", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0018581715412437916], [1421, -7.003323078155518]], [[1144, -1.2993897144042421e-05], [1902, -11.871049880981445]], [[310, -0.3937314748764038], [4087, -1.211869716644287]], [[5707, -0.7333051562309265], [4087, -1.093938946723938]], [[310, -6.6757424974639434e-06], [303, -12.566155433654785]], [[1156, -2.622607780722319e-06], [6163, -13.588669776916504]], [[25, -0.011804481036961079], [9859, -5.055246353149414]], [[328, -0.06927651911973953], [9357, -2.909513235092163]], [[7734, -4.422762503963895e-05], [2523, -10.622404098510742]], [[264, -3.635949542513117e-05], [15440, -11.063072204589844]], [[15440, -4.625427391147241e-05], [1304, -10.047057151794434]], [[6321, -7.391003236989491e-06], [15440, -13.120624542236328]], [[314, -0.014647424221038818], [2423, -4.790768623352051]], [[883, -6.9141628955549095e-0